PLANT-X for your club leader (copy into your notes):

What it is: An AI-powered early-warning system that predicts plant stress before visible symptoms appear.
Problem: Humans notice plant stress too late (after wilting/yellowing). By then, the plant has already been damaged.
Solution: Collect environmental sensor data (soil moisture, temperature, humidity, light) + plant photos, then use machine learning to find patterns that precede stress.
Innovation: Prediction, not just detection. Instead of "the soil is dry," the goal is "this plant has 84% probability of stress within 6 hours."
Demo feature: Image upload + visual assessment — researchers can photograph a plant, record health score, leaf condition, growth stage, and stress indicators without needing a live camera.
How to improve: Version 1 = sensors + basic ML. Version 2 = add prediction of future stress. Version 3 = add computer vision. Version 4 = multimodal (sensors + camera + growth data combined). Limitations: species behave differently, small datasets, false alarms possible — these are research questions, not blockers.
